# Cite the lines

Explain this repo by pointing at the code. Read the file in this turn, then cite the lines you read.

Use this fence. `startLine` and `endLine` are the line numbers from that read. The path is relative to the workspace root.

```12:15:app/review/page.tsx
// the lines this claim is about
```

One fence per region. A path in backticks, such as `app/review/page.tsx`, names the file when the claim is about the file as a whole.

The answer is done when every function, constant, route, or behavior you attribute to this repo has a fence for the lines you read. When you have not found the lines, say so and keep the answer to the lines you did locate.

General language, library, or framework facts stay uncited.
